arXiv:2610.28137v1 Announce Type: new Abstract: In this article, we reanalyze the mass and pole residue of $\Lambda$-type singly heavy baryons with spin-parity $J^P=1/2^{\pm}$ using two-point QCD sum rules. Then, we investigate the electroweak transition form factors of $\Lambda_b	o\Lambda^*_c(2595)$ and $\Xi_b	o\Xi^*_c(2790)$ within the framework of three-point QCD sum rules. At the hadron side, all possible couplings of the interpolating currents to hadronic states are taken into account, while at the QCD side, both the perturbative part and vacuum condensate contributions up to dimension-8 are included. Using the obtained form factors, we calculate the decay widths and branching ratios for the semileptonic decays $\Lambda_b	o\Lambda^*_c(2595)\ell ar{
u}_\ell$ and $\Xi_b	o\Xi^*_c(2790)\ell ar{
u}_\ell$ ($\ell=e,\mu$ and $	au$), as well as for the corresponding nonleptonic decays $\Lambda_b	o\Lambda^*_c(2595)\pi[ho]$, $\Lambda_b	o\Lambda^*_c(2595)K[K^*]$, $\Xi_b	o\Xi^*_c(2790)\pi[ho]$ and $\Xi_b	o\Xi^*_c(2790)K[K^*]$. Our predictions for the branching ratios of $\Lambda_b	o\Lambda^*_c(2595)\ell ar{
u}_\ell$ are comparable with the experimental data and other theoretical results. In addition, we present predictions for several observables, including the lepton universality ratio, the forward-backward asymmetry $A_{FB}$, and the asymmetry parameter $\alpha$, which may be useful for future experimental tests. These results can provide valuable references for future measurements.

arXiv:2607.11652v2 Announce Type: replace Abstract: We compare standard fixed-order NLO QCD predictions for the full off-shell $pp 	o e^+
u_e\, \mu^- ar{
u}_\mu\, 	au^+
u_	au\, b ar{b} \, (j) + X$ processes in the multi-lepton decay channel with the results obtained using the MiNLO approach. The MiNLO method, now also implemented in the Helac-NLO framework, provides a dynamic determination of the renormalization and factorization scale settings by identifying the most likely branching histories of the additional jets through an inverse $k_T$-clustering algorithm. The inclusion of Sudakov form factors accounts for the large logarithms that arise in the presence of widely separated scales. We perform a dedicated comparison of the two approaches at both the integrated and differential (fiducial) cross-section levels for the LHC Run II energy of $\sqrt{s}=13$ TeV. Finally, we present the merging of the full off-shell predictions for $pp 	o e^+
u_e\, \mu^- ar{
u}_\mu\, 	au^+
u_	au\, b ar{b} \, + X$, $pp 	o e^+
u_e\, \mu^- ar{
u}_\mu\, 	au^+
u_	au\, b ar{b} \, j +X$ and $pp 	o e^+
u_e\, \mu^- ar{
u}_\mu\, 	au^+
u_	au\, b ar{b} \, jj$, with the aim of improving the description of the underlying $pp 	o e^+
u_e\, \mu^- ar{
u}_\mu\, 	au^+
u_	au\, b ar{b} + X$ process.
